vo_mediacodec: MediaCodec surface output with a timed OSD plane

The whole of vo_mediacodec.c, which no upstream mpv carries. Every change
to the file lives here instead of in a follow-up patch: a follow-up applies
by context, so a version bump that breaks one would cascade through every
later one, while a single file creation cannot conflict at all. A change
that also touches upstream files keeps that side, and its write-up, in its
own patch.

Folded in, in series order:

* 0013-vo-mediacodec-request-isolated-event-prefetch:

    vo_mediacodec: request the isolated event-prefetch renderer

    The event pre-render asks sd_ass for its isolated prefetch state (patch
    0013) with OSD_DRAW_PREFETCH, and the vo.rst description of the OSD plane
    says what that buys. Split from 0013 so the sub/ half can be shared with
    the other VOs that pre-render subtitles.

* 0014-vo-mediacodec-document-compacted-atlases:

    vo_mediacodec: document compacted atlases on the OSD plane

    The vo.rst half of 0014, split from it so the sub/ half can be shared with
    the other VOs.

* 0105-vo-mediacodec-separate-preparation-and-submission
    (its vo_mediacodec.c side; the rest, and its write-up, stay in that patch)

* 0104-vo-mediacodec-live-osd-rebind

* 0106-vo-mediacodec-fill-letterbox-on-osd-plane

* 0107-vo-mediacodec-sparse-stats

* 0108-vo-mediacodec-present-feedback

* 0109-vo-mediacodec-repaint-osd-after-resize

* 0110-vo-live-window-id
    (its vo_mediacodec.c side; the rest, and its write-up, stay in that patch)

* 0112-vo-mediacodec-choreographer-refresh-rate

* 0113-vo-mediacodec-count-missed-frames

* 0114-vo-mediacodec-count-off-cadence-holds

* 0115-vo-mediacodec-own-late-frame-policy

* 0120-vo-mediacodec-distrust-render-times-off-the-vsync-clock

* 0123-vo-mediacodec-snap-to-the-choreographers-own-vsync-grid

* 0124-vo-mediacodec-hand-frames-to-the-codec-50-ms-ahead-as-media3-does

* 0127-vo-mediacodec-render-through-the-shared-osd-pipeline:

    vo_mediacodec: render subtitles through the shared osd_ahead pipeline

    The render stage, request mailbox, result queue and scheduler core moved to
    video/out/osd_ahead.c (0031); drive that module instead of a private copy.
    The GL present stage, the swap lead and the statistics lines stay here and
    read the module's state under its lock. The render thread gets the OSD
    Surface's size, the embedder's geometry (latched under the lock, as it was
    copied before) and its display priority through the module's callbacks.
    No behavior change.

* 0128-vo-mediacodec-call-the-choreographer-outside-the-sampler-lock

* 0129-vo-mediacodec-itemize-late-frame-timing:

    Subject: [PATCH] vo_mediacodec: itemize where a late frame's time went

    The video-present line counts frames released after their deadline, and
    nothing says why: a codec that decoded the frame late, a player that took
    it from the decoder late, a core that handed it to the VO late, and a VO
    thread that woke late all look the same. An Amlogic S928X box at 25 Hz
    released about one frame in eighteen late on a 1080i50 recording that
    ExoPlayer kept whole on the same codec and mode (Plezy #2485).

    For each late frame, up to 600 per VO, log one frame-timing line: the
    instant its access unit was queued to the codec, the codec reported it
    decoded, the decoder handed it over (av_mediacodec_buffer_get_timing), the
    core handed it to this VO, and it was released, each in ms against the
    frame's deadline, plus how many decoded buffers were queued behind it and
    how many the player held. One release in 250 is itemized as a sample
    whether late or not, so a late frame reads against an ordinary one. Verbose
    only, like the stats lines.

* 0130-vo-mediacodec-split-late-frame-wait-between-core-and-vo
    (its vo_mediacodec.c side; the rest, and its write-up, stay in that patch)

* 0131-player-hand-vo-mediacodec-a-frame-without-waiting-for-the-next
    (its vo_mediacodec.c side; the rest, and its write-up, stay in that patch)

* 0132-player-hold-the-video-chain-for-the-embedders-vo-switch
    (its vo_mediacodec.c side; the rest, and its write-up, stay in that patch)

