index 814e1e4..2206d5d 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/vo.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/vo.rst
@@ -723,6 +723,77 @@ Available video output drivers are:
         :yes:   Attempt to enable VRR, whether the capability is reported or not.
         :auto:  Attempt to enable VRR if support is reported.
 
+``mediacodec`` (Android)
+    Renders ``IMGFMT_MEDIACODEC`` frames directly to an ``android.view.Surface``
+    with per-frame presentation timestamps, and renders subtitles/OSD into a
+    second, transparent ``android.view.Surface``. Requires
+    ``--wid=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)`` and, for OSD/subtitles,
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-osd-surface=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)``.
+    Hardware sessions require ``--hwdec=mediacodec`` (not ``-copy``); software
+    frames are rejected, since copying them in would connect the Surface as a
+    CPU producer and prevent a GL VO from binding it later.
+
+    The embedder owns geometry: the video Surface must be sized to the
+    aspect-corrected video rectangle (decoded buffers are scaled to the whole
+    Surface), while the OSD Surface's bounds define its independent canvas and
+    must be stacked above the video. Since decoded buffers go straight to the
+    system compositor, the decoder's dataspace (HDR) is preserved and no GPU
+    pass runs on the video, but video filters and screenshots are unavailable.
+
+    The render-request mailbox is latest-wins: requests not yet serviced may
+    be replaced under load. Completed frames instead enter a four-result FIFO;
+    newer requests cannot replace queued frames or a result held by the
+    presenter. Each retains its snapshot and matching video-release timing
+    until presentation or invalidation. Only the raster worker waits for queue
+    capacity; video release does not wait. Seven CPU slots bound ownership of
+    active, queued and speculative snapshots.
+
+    Subtitles/OSD are rasterized on their own thread as soon as a frame is
+    known to the VO, pre-rendered for the next frame from the observed frame
+    cadence while the current one waits for its deadline, and, while the OSD
+    is static, for the first frame of the next subtitle event ahead of its
+    start (never past what the subtitle decoders have read). ASS event
+    pre-renders retain a separate renderer and packed atlas, so intervening
+    current-frame renders cannot evict their prepared state. At handoff only
+    the old renderer's event-layout snapshots are released; both renderers,
+    their raster/font caches and worker pools remain reusable. The exact
+    requested timestamp is rendered, including repeated requests at the same
+    timestamp: an unchanged result reuses the prepared atlas, not an image
+    accepted by age. Reset, option changes and output deselection discard the
+    pending renderer. This prefetch path is used by this Android VO; it does
+    not enable persistent libass layout caching.
+    A render that repeats the pixels already on screen is
+    folded into them and costs no swap. Glyph masks normally remain separate
+    and are composed on the GPU. Heavy overlap is flattened before upload
+    only when the masks occupy more than four times the composited RGBA
+    area in bytes; tracks requiring per-mask VSFilter color correction keep
+    their masks. Transparent pixels are skipped and opaque pixels copied
+    directly during CPU composition. Both workers use display priority.
+    Queue lookahead keeps a 50 ms/two-display-period floor and budgets two
+    source-frame intervals plus a composition display period, capped at 500 ms.
+    Rasterized frames are uploaded while the present thread is idle, and
+    presented through a GLES2 surface over the OSD Surface with the same
+    presentation timestamp the video buffer got, so both latch on one vsync.
+    The video is never held back for the OSD: under load subtitle updates
+    are skipped or shown late instead. A ``osd-sync`` line in the verbose log
+    every 120 frames and at exit reports render times, pre-render hits, how
+    many frames were uploaded and composed ahead of their draw, late swaps
+    and, where the compositor supports ``EGL_ANDROID_get_frame_timestamps``,
+    where swaps actually landed.
+
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-video-rect=<vw>,<vh>,<left>,<top>,<right>,<bottom>``
+    supplies the applied video rectangle relative to the full OSD view.
+    The six signed decimal integers are updated atomically at runtime.
+    Viewport dimensions must be positive and right/bottom are exclusive;
+    negative margins are supported for zoom. Empty (the default) means that
+    geometry is unavailable. Invalid updates retain the last valid geometry.
+
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-osd-vsync-delay=<0..3>`` (default 0) presents the OSD
+    that many display periods after the video's timestamp. Some hardware
+    codec paths put the picture on screen a vsync after a GL layer given the
+    same timestamp; the embedder supplies the offset it measured. Only the
+    presentation time is shifted, the rendered pts is not.
+
